    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d363">

                <pb facs="0577" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">612.1123/141a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-03-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 13, 1915</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: I am sending you a copy
                    of the telegram in regard to Progreso.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d363-f1"/> I feel as
                    reluctant as you do to take such positive action, but I believe it as real a
                    kindness to Carranza as it was to Huerta and I think the Huerta incident
                    furnishes a very strong precedent. While Carranza <hi rendition="#underline"
                        >may</hi> take offense at it, the chances are he will not, and we can assure
                    Villa and Zapata of our purposes, and in case we came in conflict with Carranza
                    we are in a position to restrain the employment of force within the smallest
                    possible limit just as we did at Vera Cruz. At Progreso there would be no reason
                    for landing a force or taking charge of the port. The people of Progreso are
                    against Carranza, while at Vera Cruz Huerta was in possession.</p>
                <pb facs="0578" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/>
                <p>As Mr. McAdoo told you, I am preparing to leave for Atlantic City at four o’clock
                    this afternoon. Mr. Davis will telephone me if anything comes up that might
                    require my presence here.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. J. Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
